## How to write an entry

One line for the decision, one for the reason, and a link if there is more to say. The essay belongs in `docs/dev/` — this file stays skimmable.

If a decision departs from a `.claude/guidelines/` file, **name the guideline**. That makes it a settled deviation: `/plan` applies it and stops re-asking. A contradiction that does not name what it contradicts looks like an accident and gets queried every time.

Archive superseded entries under `## Superseded` at the bottom rather than deleting them — a reversed decision is itself information — and keep them out of the topic index.

